---
/* /how-i-build — D57 clause 9: the engineering model, from VERIFIED practice
 * evidence only (docs/evidence/practice/). The cross-review claim is
 * REPORTED with its own "do not publish yet" bar in cross-review.md and is
 * deliberately absent from this page — nothing here cites that file.
 *
 * Every claim's key term is bound to a line inside its evidence file that
 * follows that file's own `VERIFIED` marker (how-i-build.spec.js) — not a
 * file-wide contains-check, which cannot distinguish a VERIFIED claim from
 * a REPORTED one living in the same file (package-5 plan, testcheck lens).
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Plate from '../components/Plate.astro';
import '../styles/how-i-build.css';
/* .plate-grid.one-col / .plate-copy.wide — RCA-013: same dead-class defect
   as /experience, same fix (see that page's comment and one-col.css). */
import '../styles/one-col.css';

/* Pinned at quorum-ai's main HEAD when this citation was added (RCA-012).
   A const keeps the URL under the 120-char line ceiling — file-budget.mjs
   has no exception recorded for this file, so the line is split instead. */
const WATCHDOG_SHA = 'ec4a4b987b22214b74bd11d03d4c682aed317271';
const WATCHDOG_URL = `https://github.com/imrohitagrawal/quorum-ai/blob/${WATCHDOG_SHA}`
  + '/.github/workflows/deploy-drift-watchdog.yml';
---

<Layout
  title="How I build — Rohit Agrawal"
  description="An engineering practice built as reusable, versioned instructions, CI
    that knows blocking from advisory, and tooling built from named incidents —
    verified against the repositories, not described from memory."
>
  <Plate id="how-i-build">
    <div class="plate-grid one-col">
      <div class="plate-copy wide">
        <h1 class="plate-title tight">How I build.</h1>

        {/* RCA-015 (P5): the artefact sits ABOVE the claim bands, not after
            them. It used to arrive fourth, and P2's own accuracy fix — making
            this quote genuinely verbatim — made it taller, pushing its most
            important line past the fold: at 390x844 the fold landed ON the
            words "This is a PROXY", so a phone reader got the watchdog's claim
            and none of its stated limit. Hoisted, the whole panel clears the
            fold with 167.2px to spare. Owner's ruling P-28: the quote is NOT
            shortened — that would reverse P2 — the panel moves instead.
            Gated by tests/viewport-reach.spec.js. */}
        <blockquote class="artefact">
          <p>
            &ldquo;It fixes the failure mode we hit on #54: main got a new commit but no
            deploy fired (a dropped Actions event / skipped-or-failed deploy gate / a
            flake), leaving prod stale with no one watching.&rdquo;
          </p>
          <p>
            &ldquo;WHAT IT CHECKS (honest scope) [...] the deploy JOB, not a /health
            200 [...] This is a PROXY: it cannot see a Deploy run that reported
            success while production did not actually roll [...] on 2026-08-07 that
            left production 34m31s behind while every passive probe stayed
            green.&rdquo;
          </p>
          <footer>
            <a href={WATCHDOG_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            >deploy-drift-watchdog.yml, quorum-ai</a>
          </footer>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="model-band">
          <p class="band-lead">
            Reusable, versioned instructions — for requirements and security, not only code.
          </p>
          <p class="band-support">
            113 <span class="band-term">authored skill</span> directories, including skills
            that route between the others and audit anything adopted from outside.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="model-band">
          <p class="band-lead">
            CI that knows which checks can stop a release and which only inform it.
          </p>
          <p class="band-support">
            One workflow's own comment: a golden-set gate is hermetic and <span
              class="band-term"
            >blocking</span>; a latency baseline is advisory.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="model-band">
          <p class="band-lead">
            Tooling built from named incidents — a deploy-watchdog opens with <span
              class="band-term"
            >the incident that caused it</span>.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </Plate>

  <Plate id="evals-observability">
    <div class="plate-grid one-col">
      <div class="plate-copy wide">
        <h2 class="plate-title tight">Evals and observability, specifically.</h2>

        <div class="model-band">
          <p class="band-lead">
            A calibration harness and a drift test that both admit their own limits.
          </p>
          <p class="band-support">
            Judge agreement scored with Cohen's κ, PABAK, and Spearman correlation — the labels
            it checks against are <span class="band-term">explicitly not blind human labels</span>,
            its own decision record says so. Separately, a Kolmogorov&ndash;Smirnov test watches
            live output against a stored baseline, with an <span class="band-term"
            >alert on a floor breach</span> — demo-proven, not yet wired to live traffic.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="model-band">
          <p class="band-lead">
            Tracing with the secrets stripped, and two ways of separating a blocking gate from
            an advisory one.
          </p>
          <p class="band-support">
            OpenTelemetry and Prometheus across two systems, secrets removed <span
              class="band-term"
            >before it leaves the process</span>. One repo's judged eval only runs on a pull
            request <span class="band-term">labelled full-eval</span>, since it costs real
            money; another enforces a fixture-backed eval suite as one of eleven contexts
            checked live against the branch-protection API.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Plate>

  <Plate id="published-skills">
    <div class="plate-grid one-col">
      <div class="plate-copy wide">
        <h2 class="plate-title tight">Published, not just practiced.</h2>
        <p>
          One of the skills above is a public repository — the instructions themselves,
          not a description of them.
        </p>
        <ul class="skill-repos">
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/imrohitagrawal/project-doc-skills"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >project-doc-skills</a>{' '}
            — architecture-and-decisions and doc-critic, the two skills behind this
            site's own documentation practice.
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href="https://github.com/imrohitagrawal/.github"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener"
            >.github</a>{' '}
            — the contribution and security templates every other repository here
            inherits from, not a skill.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/experience">Career evolution</a>
          <a class="btn primary" href="mailto:rohit.ra.agrawal@gmail.com">Email me</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Plate>
</Layout>
